# YTV media: the file channels' media folders out of Nextcloud's data directory, served as
# plain HTTP for the televisions. Port 4244, ufw-limited to the LAN and tailscale0 - there is
# no auth on this, so the path list below IS the entire exposure. It is generated from the
# file_*.json confs' media_dir fields at deploy time (deploy.sh swaps the placeholder line
# inside the site block below for the matcher - the token must not appear anywhere else in
# this file, or a second matcher lands outside the site block and Caddy refuses it, as it
# did 2026-09-09..16): adding a
# channel adds exactly one more folder's reach, and Nothing Else.
#
# Caddy because it was already installed on the box and speaks Range requests out of the box -
# both players issue bounded byte ranges for everything (see ChunkedDataSource/ChunkedProxy in
# the app), and a static server without Range support makes Media3 read the whole file as one
# request.
#
# The files are owned by http (Nextcloud's user) and this runs as http too: read-only serving
# of exactly the directories Nextcloud already owns. Nothing here lets Caddy write.

:4244 {
	root * /mnt/hdd/nextcloud-data/data/hermanb/files

@@PATHS@@
	# Everything else - the files root, Music, directory listings - does not exist here.
	handle {
		respond 404
	}
}
